{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand","id":991665,"title":"The most \"Practical\" Tradition and the most \"Hard\" to play/understand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-22T19:47:46-07:00","id":991665,"title":"The most \"Practical\" Tradition and the most \"Hard\" to play/understand","content":"So..who do you think is the most &quot;practical&quot; tradition, when it comes to ideals, organization, practices, rootes etc...and which is the &quot;hardest&quot; to get in your own opinion?<br /> <br /> personally...the hollow ones on my case, i really think they adapted pretty well to modern times and i love the way they work.<br /> <br /> the hardest on my end is the Akashic Brotherhood, to me its a bit perhaps cliche the &quot;magic martial artist&quot; so , i think they are pretty ..how to put it...dont mesh well with some traditions when it comes to certain games (i try to keep them away, besides i think Do is way to overpowerful, but thats just personal opinion)<br /> <br /> what about ya?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T20:10:52-07:00","id":991676,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of people miss the point of the Cult of Ecstasy beyond being the crazy sex and drugs Tradition, and it's a damn shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:15:56-07:00","id":991715,"title":"","content":"The Order of Hermes. I get what they are about in theory, but in practice it's really complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:19:49-07:00","id":991717,"title":"","content":"Virtual Adepts are definitely the most practical. The least would probably be the Order of Hermes, with their need for vast libraries and rare materials.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:34:56-07:00","id":991728,"title":"","content":"Verbena are traditionally the most practical, and many of them use blood magic, so they only need a razor as a tool. Sons of Ether are impractical because you need a van's worth of tools to do anything. I still like them though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T22:45:29-07:00","id":991731,"title":"","content":"The Verbana are among the most practical, which is kind of the point. Witchcraft is an eminently practical art, developed by peasantry to make their lives easier. Many of their tools are common household items.<br /> <br /> Now, I love the Order of Hermes. It's my personal favorite Tradition. That said, it's magical style is easy to explain on the surface but complicated as hell to get into. Part of this because they don't just draw on one magical system, but several different ones, that in turn bleed into one another. Alchemy, Astrology, Theurgy, Kabbala, Tarot, Enochian (not just a language, but a system of magick unto itself), and ceremonial magics from Egypt, Babylon, Greece, Rome, Persia, and Sumer. Explaining any one aspect of Hermetic theory would provide more than enough material for an Order of Hermes character, let alone all of them. And this not even getting into how popular depictions of wizards blend into the mix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T00:08:28-07:00","id":991761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=991728#post991728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Verbena are traditionally the most practical, and many of them use blood magic, so they only need a razor as a tool. Sons of Ether are impractical because you need a van's worth of tools to do anything. I still like them though.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Sons of Ether at least we've all been training how to do them properly by watching thousands of movies and TV shows about mad scientists and nutty professors, as well as semi-serious stuff about ancient astronauts and other far-out theories.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes is a whole other level of hard to grasp, because they haven't been fleshed out nearly as much. While the popular image of wizards is rooted in them, almost nothing about them other than the general look has made it into the popular consciousness. Understanding the Order of Hermes takes research on a level much greater than the Sons of Ether.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:33:28-07:00","id":991778,"title":"","content":"i have found that decades of kung fu movies and fighting games leads many new players to finding the Akashic Brotherhood easy to get into. if they dont get it after a double feature of Iron Monkey and Kung Fu hustle (or a night of street fighter and mortal combat for that matter) there is no hope. find a new trad. <br /> I also agree about the OofH. the homework is nuts. but when you DO get it its a whole new game. im still wrapping my head around the things you can do with thoughtforms and astral manipulation. as above so below sounds so simple when you say it...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T02:55:59-07:00","id":991787,"title":"","content":"No ones said it yet, so here it is.<br /> <br /> I love the Euthanatos, but I always find that they are the hardest tradition to pin down. It could be because of a lack of experience with Hinduism, but I remember struggling the most with understanding how they translate their eight spoked wheel into magical practice.<br /> I still have trouble thinking about their paradigm at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:12:19-07:00","id":991841,"title":"","content":"Doing the Celestial Chorus without acting like a stereotypical fantasy cleric or an offensive pastiche of Christianity can be pretty hard in my expericence.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, on the other side, we have the Syndicate who require that you read through books filled with economic theories before you can do something more nuanced than: &quot;I HAVE MORE RESOURCES DOTS THAN YOU HAVE DOTS IN TOTAL! BOW TO ME INFERIOR CREATURES!&quot;<br /> <br /> NWO can also be pretty hard, especially the Ivory Tower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T09:50:44-07:00","id":991882,"title":"","content":"I find the Hermetics most approachable since they're the closest to the Urban Fantasy Mage you get with Harry Potter, Dresden Files, etc. and Verbena the hardest because they're all about stabbing themselves and bleeding on everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:19:45-07:00","id":991893,"title":"","content":"Personally, Sons of Ether are easy to understand. Non-Reductionist science. You just go around doing science WITHOUT assuming that everyone else is wrong. So they essentially play like a Technocrat, only their theories don't need to fit together as much which makes stuff easier.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Cult of Ecstasy.... yeah. They just don't make any sense to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T10:52:19-07:00","id":991908,"title":"","content":"Orphans can be both the most practical and the hardest \u201cTradition\u201c.<br /> <br /> You can literally copy the Focus of one of the Harry's.<br /> And you can build everything from scrap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:53:32-07:00","id":991965,"title":"","content":"Hermetics are easiest to understand because they do what most people consider to be magic. Euthanatos is the hardest because their conception of enlightenment and what kind of magic that allows them to do is beyond what most people are familiar.<br /> <br /> The thing I found about Mage is that many players really don't get that the magic they can must fit within the paradigm of their tradition. Instead, they got the sphere ratings up to what they want them to be, and want to be D&amp;D style wizards.<br /> <br /> The WoD games are all designed to allow narrative play and are not the most mechanically minded RPG game, but Mage really requires STs and Players to be story first and mechanics second. That means at times not doing things mechanically you are allowed to do, if you can't justify it according to your paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:33:02-07:00","id":991988,"title":"","content":"I've actually done a fair bit of research into the Order of Hermes, and yet at this moment I couldn't tell you much about them except their theology reminded me a fair bit of Scientology. Their beliefs are so complex and arcane that it takes a lot of study to both learn it AND memorize it well enough to play it properly and consistently. Sure, the pointy hats, wands, and latinesque chants are easy enough, but it's a pain beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:13:50-07:00","id":992001,"title":"","content":"All Traditions can be an universe unto themselves when you look deep enough, so it isn't what bothers me. I actualy find the Akashic Brotherhood fairly simple. And Do isn't all that strong, nor really necessary, you can do with just Brawl and fluff. What makes them good fighters, when they are, is to use Do as Foci (I still use Revised). But other traditions can do the same, so no big deal, just make your chainsaw into a Focus and be happy.<br /> <br /> The hardest for me is the Syndicate, by far. How economy translates to magic is the real conudrum for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:24:00-07:00","id":992011,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12022_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12022\" data-vbnamecard=\"12022\">Nonsense</a> is right, but it applies to all the Mage organizations.<br /> <br /> Every one of the Traditions/Crafts/Conventions has a 'surface' level of play at which they are actually completely functional and practical, and a 'deep' level of play that delves far more into complex and arcane philosophies, beliefs, and so on.<br /> <br /> There's no Tradition that's actually &quot;easier&quot; than others, or harder, because they're all designed to take a fairly simple archetype and then pile on depth to the level you enjoy playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:43:55-07:00","id":992024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=991787#post991787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No ones said it yet, so here it is.<br /> <br /> I love the Euthanatos, but I always find that they are the hardest tradition to pin down. It could be because of a lack of experience with Hinduism, but I remember struggling the most with understanding how they translate their eight spoked wheel into magical practice.<br /> I still have trouble thinking about their paradigm at times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. And it's all that much harder because the Euthanatos are probably the most &quot;made up&quot; group in game. The various constituent groups were a veritable grab bag of different cultures and parts of other mystic groups. It's not just Chakravanti. They might be the most numerous, but it's not even close to being a majority. There's the remnants of the more sepulchral of the Greek Mystery Religions. There's the Madzimbabwe that were &quot;willing to come out and play&quot;. And so on. It's really hard to see how anything representing a group identity would have gelled out even in the past several centuries. They just don't all have any one thing in common, though they all have something in common with another group. Leading to a sort of loose, floppy blanket of a continuum identity that doesn't really help in situating a player when the approach the group. Particularly when the &quot;easy&quot; answer is probably the worst answer &quot;necromancer assassins&quot;. It's unapproachable. There is no real cultural touchstone or source to point to help out with that. Especially since Mage magic is very very weak with regard to whole modern &quot;necromancy&quot; schtick. The Spheres are just bad building blocks to set up those kinds of effects, and they feel very much off. And then there is all the thematic cross-over with the Verbena.... Cycles and death and life, etc. To the point that it seems like Nightshade was just being kinda a bitch and forcing groups that seem like they should have been Verbena away from &quot;the cool kid's table&quot; of the Verbena and forcing them to go sit with all the emo and strange kids over at the Euthanatos/Chakravanti table. (There is some deep seeded Eurocentrism in the creation of the Nine Traditions that makes some historical sense, but it does lead to balky situations.)<br /> <br /> Oh, and having Entropy as a Sphere doesn't help either, as the powers of the Sphere don't really seem to mesh with either the superficial conceptions or more nuanced ones. (Nope, the Orphics, the Madzimbabwe nor the Chakrtavanti were known for their extraordinary luck, the ability to inflict precision damage, making things fall apart, etc.) Not that other Traditions don't have similar issues... (Celestial Chorus and the very Hermetic Platonic Prime as written, etc.) but all of the above plus that exacerbates the situation.<br /> <br /> Not that I don't love.them. My favoirte Mage PC ever and some of my favorite NPCs all the way back to the weirdness of First Edition have been Euthanatos. But it hasn't really ever been easy. <br /> <br /> The group I have seen the least number of people willing to tackle has been the Celestial Chorus. And that has included myself as ST and player to some degree.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it's all over the board. It depends on the person and their attachment to the role and their character conception. One player did the Celestial Chorus pretty well when she created a character whose tagline was &quot;the nun with a gun&quot; (actually two guns as it turned out.... often machine pistols.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T18:57:50-07:00","id":992165,"title":"","content":"Kind of why I prefer the Foundations/Pillars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T19:45:27-07:00","id":992185,"title":"","content":"<b>Most Practical:</b> most of the Technocracy. We live in their reality, don't we?<br /> <br /> <b>Hard to Play/Understand:</b> Probably the $yndicate, though some parts of the Virtual Adepts and most of the Euthanatoi are pretty close.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=991841#post991841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Meanwhile, on the other side, we have the Syndicate who require that you read through books filled with economic theories before you can do something more nuanced than: &quot;I HAVE MORE RESOURCES DOTS THAN YOU HAVE DOTS IN TOTAL! BOW TO ME INFERIOR CREATURES!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of the $yndicate paradigm has to deal with the fact that modern money is based off of the consensual belief that money (small metal disks and paper) have <b>value.</b> They are <b>important</b>, but only because everyone thinks so. They are <b>important</b> because everyone wants them. If you control what everyone wants and the Prime motivator of (most) human choice/action, then you can control Reality.<br /> <br /> Example: I have hypereconomics, so I know how to leverage peoples' desires and ability to make what I want Real. Through buying/selling at the speed of the internet (Ebay), I can change this can of Chef Boyardee into a block of reinforced concrete. I bought it, the money was deducted from my account, I hit the right buttons on Ebay, there are several receipts and bank transactions showing that the 34 deals were made, therefore<b> this can of Chef Boyardee is now a block of reinforced concrete.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10653-omegaz","name":"OmegaZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10653_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T21:04:36-07:00","id":992230,"title":"","content":"It shed some light on them.<br /> <br /> But so little that I still want badly to read their Convention Book (never had the chance).<br /> <br /> That's a shame, actualy. I really love economy and really want to understand the Syndicate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T22:05:06-07:00","id":992263,"title":"","content":"One of the advantages of being part of a Convention is that you are trained to depend on mundane solutions instead of magical solutions. That makes the Technocrats easy to play because Enlightened Citizens are going to use the same methods as Extraordinary Citizens the majority of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:21:47-07:00","id":992391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=992263#post992263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the advantages of being part of a Convention is that you are trained to depend on mundane solutions instead of magical solutions. That makes the Technocrats easy to play because Enlightened Citizens are going to use the same methods as Extraordinary Citizens the majority of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's even easier if you have a degree in their specific areas of influence.<br /> <br /> NWO: Psychology, Sociology, and Political studies.<br /> Syndicate: Economics, Finance, Business studies and Media studies<br /> Progenitors: Biology (including Genetics, Biochemistry, Ecology, Immunology, etc) and Organic Chemistry<br /> Iteration X: Engineering, Physics (Mostly Newtonian) Mechanics, Computing, Robotics, and Inorganic Chemistry<br /> Void Engineers: Physics (Quantum physics, Astrophysics) and Astronomy.<br /> <br /> Conversely, not knowing anything about these subjects is going to make it an absolute pain to play as these guys.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if you happen to have been involved in Wiccan rituals or have a Pagan upbringing, Verbena are going to feel much more intuitive. Similarly a Christian upbringing may make it easier to apply specific rituals from Christianity into your magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T12:10:05-07:00","id":992520,"title":"","content":"Yes. In my case, it would be quite easy to play NWO, Syndicate, or Void Engineers because I have degrees that overlap within those fields (interdisciplinary degrees are occasionally useful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:02:56-07:00","id":992561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=992263#post992263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the advantages of being part of a Convention is that you are trained to depend on mundane solutions instead of magical solutions. That makes the Technocrats easy to play because Enlightened Citizens are going to use the same methods as Extraordinary Citizens the majority of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not. As it is a lot harder than it looks to come up with a decent effect and attached Instruments. The fact it is so mundane and must be so mundane often makes it too mundane to be extraordinary and/or immediately, decisively useful. It takes a much harder transition to &quot;mage casting thinking&quot; than with the more supernatural ways of reality-alteration as it doesn't just involve learning something (e.g. how to take these rules and use these ideas to allow my character to do extraordinary things), it involves un-learning normalcy, learning how to take normal things to do not-normal things and still making it all appear to be normal. There's a lot of mental gymnastics involved and, like actual gymnastics, it takes talent and work. Technocrats seem to have a hard learning curve until they &quot;get&quot; their characters that I haven't seen with SoE or Verbena or Hermetics or whatever. Once they can do the three-way mental flip-flop, they seem to love it, but early on there ends up being a lot of &quot;Why should I even bother doing &quot;magic&quot; for this, when it's effectively just something that can be done with an Ability+Attribute roll...&quot;<br /> <br /> And this is especially true with the Syndicate and N.W.O. It-X, Progenitors and VE can be a lot easier overall as they lend themselves to a similar mindset to running any other technomancer.<br /> <br /> Extraordinary Citizens are a lot easier with a really tight bag of tricks. It's not that hard to be Bond with a sackful of cool do-dads, but it's a lot harder to be Bond/Q who improvises like a maestro and creates new stuff, methods, actions and reactions on the spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:22:38-07:00","id":992567,"title":"","content":"Practical: Any faction of a Tradition that has the word &quot;Techno&quot; in it.<br /> <br /> Hardest for me to understand: Verbena, but this is mostly because I don't buy into Wicca as a universalist Paradigm. Between the Euthanatos, Chorus, Dreamspeakers and Cultists I don't see how the Verbena stand out asside from being politically annoying at the Council of Nine. VA is a close second because I'm not sure they couldn't be a faction of the SOE and not miss much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T17:16:45-07:00","id":992641,"title":"","content":"Well, I find the distinction between VA and SoE quite easy to figure out. Actualy, the VA doesn't even have to bother with science at all if they don't want to. It is a paradigm about Information, about the universe-as-data, and about data being translated and transformed through computing logic. The SoE are all about <u>not</u> defining too hard a paradigm. About science as an ethos of research without barriers to the theories you create. Ultimately, about reallity made of creating ever more naturalistic possibilities instead of using knowledge to limit possibilities.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are superpositions between them. But that can be said of any two Traditions/Conventions. I can easily think of almost any naturalistic Tradition and all of the Conventions being just a faction of the SoE. Actually, I could even say that the entire Union is made of factions of the SoE, it wouldn't be too far a stretch of their history. By the way, those same groups could all be called factions of the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> The ways those groups overlap are as interesting as the ways they distinguish themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T20:18:58-07:00","id":992725,"title":"","content":"For me the eaisest to wrap my head around is the Celestial Chorus. Their core concept is monotheism which growing up Catholic is something I can wrap my head around pretty easily. The hardest for me is probably the Virtual Adepts. How computers translate into reality altering magic is beyond me. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5767-deedee","name":"DeeDee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T01:32:42-07:00","id":992849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=992641#post992641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I find the distinction between VA and SoE quite easy to figure out. Actualy, the VA doesn't even have to bother with science at all if they don't want to. It is a paradigm about Information, about the universe-as-data, and about data being translated and transformed through computing logic. The SoE are all about <u>not</u> defining too hard a paradigm. About science as an ethos of research without barriers to the theories you create. Ultimately, about reallity made of creating ever more naturalistic possibilities instead of using knowledge to limit possibilities..</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am saying I feel SOE and to an extent Hermetics could pick up the conceptual space the VAs sit in without much changing. Yes their paradigm is somewhat different but you have Druids, Voodun, Hindu Death Cultists, Greek Cthonic worshipers all stuffed into the Euthanatos.<br /> <br /> I also think the Cerimonial factions(OOH, Wu Lung etc) could have been a single group but they were all far too powerful and political for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:49:05-07:00","id":992875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/991665-the-most-practical-tradition-and-the-most-hard-to-play-understand?p=992849#post992849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the Cerimonial factions(OOH, Wu Lung etc) could have been a single group but they were all far too powerful and political for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>House Hong Lei of the Order of Hermes is basically members of Wu Lung who gave up on political differences and sought the safety of being in a larger and more dominant tradition.<br /> <br /> Other members of Wu Lung joined their ancient rivals, the Akashic Brotherhood, not wishing to bow down to a western ideology.<br /> <br /> Though I don't have any sources to confirm this, it's not unlikely that there would be those of Wu Lung who still consider the Akashics as damaging, and would rather go against them than serve along side them, yet still wish to join a larger tradition for protection and not have to go to the indignity of submitting to a Western influence. In which case they may join the Eastern arm of the Euthanatos, whom are still at odds with members of the China bound Akashics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-25-2016, 06:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T03:52:22-07:00","id":992876,"title":"","content":"Think of a character that works through wrighting stuff in paper. Her magic come from phylosophical conclusions about things. She wrights things as premises and arguments, and change reallity by describing through logic their new states.<br /> <br /> Of course, with time and practice the character becomes ever more adept at doing this, and the arguments and logical constructs become more complex. She devises mental exercises of logic to demonstrate, going from only writen material to thought exercises, roleplaying games and complex imaginary reallities, both standalone and overlaping the visible world, in a concept similar to Augmented Reallity Games (that don't need any device aside the disposition of the players to play along).<br /> <br /> There came exercises in shared reallity, where description and socializing makes for some things becoming &quot;true to an extend&quot; to some people just for being shared information. And this is precisely the notion of Virtual. It can be achieved without any device. Actualy, our hobby does precisely that, creates Virtual reallities. The game itself is a virtual reallity.<br /> <br /> I don't have time to go further, but it is just a thought exercise, there's no problem in not geting the VAs, or finding them too SoE-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T04:15:52-07:00","id":992881,"title":"","content":"I think that's the best thing about the Traditions, They are a collection of so many different facets of human belief and ingenuity. There will be factions that have views which you can understand, those that seem indistinguishable from another groups, and those that are just plain weird and alien to you.<br /> What's great is this sort of thing is reflected in the game itself. Most Hermetics don't distinguish between the many varied techniques, cultures, and ideas that go behind the huge collection of faiths that make up the Dreamspeaker tradition. That's why they've been lumped together in one big category though, because it was the Hermetics that started giving out the seats.<br /> <br /> Similarly, most mystics might have trouble distinguishing between the VA's and the Etherites. Their seats were more a question of timing than of paradigm difference. Both of them were originally Technocrats, one left before the sleeper war and the other during the aftermath of the sleeper war when the Traditions were desperate for any kind of intelligence for their own Ascension war.<br /> <br /> But if you're within the faction that you're in, those that others ascribe as &quot;similar&quot; to you seem to be worlds apart. This seen in the many competing theories in the Society of Ether, the great and divergent houses of the Order of Hermes, the constantly bickering Choristors.<br /> <br /> The Chorus has a huge number of differing beliefs and philosophies, even in just the Christian parts. There are the Septarians who denounce anything that isn't strictly Christian and see the Chorus as the one true tradition, the Monists who are much more open minded about about the interpretation of faith and consider all beliefs in monotheism to be equally valid, and the Latitudinarians who are radical reformists that think the very nature of the Chorus is biased towards the Christian faith and must be dismantled and built up from scratch in order ever meet the needs of the Tradition as a whole.<br /> <br /> Yet to the outside, they're all just &quot;The Celestial Chorus&quot;, they are all the same &quot;The One&quot; worshipping, prayer making, choir girls and boys. Equally indistinct.<br /> <br /> Going the extra mile, there are many within the Technocracy that doesn't even distinguish between the Traditions at all. Some may see them as a group of outdated ideas and baseless rhetoric. Possibly only distinguishing between Technomages, and Technology haters, of which every tradition has a couple, (yes there are even anit-tech Etherites who long for the days of steam and pipes rather than all this computerised garbage. Similarly there may be VAs who think The Net and data in general should be entirely virtual and having a computer or smart phone as a conduit is outdated and only holding humanity back.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T16:37:30-07:00","id":993171,"title":"","content":"It's simply lovable.<br /> <br /> But if their timing of entrance had a lot to do with it, the fact is that their seats are among the most perfectly matched in the Traditions. Matter says a lot about the Etherites and their approach to their ideas about science. And even more than that, the link between the VA and the Correspondence Sphere is just the best match in the game. More than any other group, the Adepts explain the further concepts behind Correspondence, and why it isn't Space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}